{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7cfa748986422e63","name":"card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/Homefront/units/card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"IS II 1944 EARLY","text":"Destruction: Add two 42nd RIFLES. Give one Guard, the other Shock.","flavorText":"Introduced in 1944, the IS-2 was the Soviet Union’s answer to heavily armored German tanks like the Panther and Tiger. Officially designated as the Iosif Stalin II, the tank featured a powerful 122 mm D-25T gun capable of knocking out enemy armor at long ranges. Unlike earlier Soviet tanks, the IS-2 emphasized armor and firepower over speed. Its frontal armor, up to 120 mm-thick and sloped, proved highly resistant to German anti-tank weapons. By mid-1944, IS-2 units were entering combat in significant numbers, particularly during the Lvov-Sandomierz Offensive. Their arrival caused concern among German commanders who recognized the tank’s ability to breach fortified positions. The IS-2’s high-explosive shells were also devastating against bunkers and infantry, making it valuable in both tank duels and urban assaults. Around 2,252 IS-2 tanks were produced in the year 1944 alone, forming the backbone of Soviet breakthrough tank regiments for the rest of the war.","faction":"Soviet","type":"tank","rarity":"Unique","cost":10,"operationCost":1,"attack":7,"defense":7},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.bond"],"Name":"card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944_title","SourceString":"IS II 1944 EARLY","LocalizedString":"IS II 1944 EARLY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":7,"defense":7,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredits":10,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944_text","SourceString":"Destruction: Add two 42nd RIFLES. Give one Guard, the other Shock.","LocalizedString":"Destruction: Add two 42nd RIFLES. Give one Guard, the other Shock."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944_history","SourceString":"Introduced in 1944, the IS-2 was the Soviet Union’s answer to heavily armored German tanks like the Panther and Tiger. Officially designated as the Iosif Stalin II, the tank featured a powerful 122 mm D-25T gun capable of knocking out enemy armor at long ranges. Unlike earlier Soviet tanks, the IS-2 emphasized armor and firepower over speed. Its frontal armor, up to 120 mm-thick and sloped, proved highly resistant to German anti-tank weapons. By mid-1944, IS-2 units were entering combat in significant numbers, particularly during the Lvov-Sandomierz Offensive. Their arrival caused concern among German commanders who recognized the tank’s ability to breach fortified positions. The IS-2’s high-explosive shells were also devastating against bunkers and infantry, making it valuable in both tank duels and urban assaults. Around 2,252 IS-2 tanks were produced in the year 1944 alone, forming the backbone of Soviet breakthrough tank regiments for the rest of the war.","LocalizedString":"Introduced in 1944, the IS-2 was the Soviet Union’s answer to heavily armored German tanks like the Panther and Tiger. Officially designated as the Iosif Stalin II, the tank featured a powerful 122 mm D-25T gun capable of knocking out enemy armor at long ranges. Unlike earlier Soviet tanks, the IS-2 emphasized armor and firepower over speed. Its frontal armor, up to 120 mm-thick and sloped, proved highly resistant to German anti-tank weapons. By mid-1944, IS-2 units were entering combat in significant numbers, particularly during the Lvov-Sandomierz Offensive. Their arrival caused concern among German commanders who recognized the tank’s ability to breach fortified positions. The IS-2’s high-explosive shells were also devastating against bunkers and infantry, making it valuable in both tank duels and urban assaults. Around 2,252 IS-2 tanks were produced in the year 1944 alone, forming the backbone of Soviet breakthrough tank regiments for the rest of the war."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","hasDestruction":true,"heavyArmor":2,"hasShock":true,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_42nd_rifles","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/IS_II_1944_EARLY.IS_II_1944_EARLY","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944_photo","SourceString":"A column of Soviet IS-2 tanks in Berlin, 1945.","LocalizedString":"A column of Soviet IS-2 tanks in Berlin, 1945."},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionArmourL'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionArmourL.36"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeHeavy_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeHeavy.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Tanks/BP_AttackTank.BP_AttackTank_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944","owner":"card_unit_iosef_stalin_ii_1944_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_text_Variable","type":"FText","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_text_Variable_1","type":"FText","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_killer","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_TriggerNotDestroyed","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetCardsInSupportLineBySide_cards","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Length_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_SpawnCardonBattlefield_spawnedCardID","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetCardsInSupportLineBySide_cards_1","type":"TArray<UBaseCard